{
 "note": "R118 (Players 3.2; phase-3 matrix: six-bit rating scale \"+50 inferred, provisional\" on NHL 08-10, \"+36 provisional\" on NHL 11-13) - a\ncross-title continuity test that does not read any single title's distribution in isolation. The same skater appears in adjacent titles;\nif displayed ratings are roughly continuous from one season to the next, the median raw difference of matched players over the shared\nsix-bit rating fields estimates off(A) - off(B). Controls with independently known offsets: NHL 14 -> 15 and NHL 15 -> Legacy (both +36 in\ngame), X360 NHL 15 -> PS4 NHL 15 (PS4 stores 0..99 with offset 0; expected about +36 if the ratings are the same season's data), NHL 07 is\n+50 in game. Year-to-year rating change of real players is the noise; the controls measure it.\n\nMatching: exhibition player bio (`ubPc`) x exhibition skater ratings (`dSvy`) by `game_id` (PS4: the first shared id field of\ngame_id / playerid). Key = (first name, last name, calendar month, calendar day) using the measured index base (1-based NHL 07-10,\n0-based NHL 11+; R116); keys that occur twice in a title are dropped. Fields = rating fields by Studio's own rule (prefix p_ / g_ / c_, declared 0..63 or 0..99; not fighting,\nstyle, paddledown, potential; overall also excluded), matched by suffix across titles.\nOptional second argument `goalie` runs the same test on `exhibitiongoalieai` (goalie rating table `mHuy`).\nRead-only. Usage: python r118_rating_offset_continuity.py <out.json> [goalie]\n",
 "rating_table": "exhibitionskaterai",
